    {
      "kind": "request",
      "text": "Help me plan my study time for the Applied Data Ethics case memo over the next two weeks. Which deadline should we plan around? I have a module outline and a learning platform export. Check my calendar and ask what times work for me before making a proposal."
    },
    {
      "kind": "question",
      "id": "availability",
      "groupId": "intake",
      "text": "Given your current calendar commitments (Mon 2026-11-02: 18:30-21:30 Evening class, 17:30-18:30 Travel to campus, 12:00-13:00 Lunch and transition, 08:00-12:00 Part-time work; Tue 2026-11-03: 12:00-13:00 Lunch and transition, 08:00-12:00 Part-time work; Wed 2026-11-04: 18:30-21:30 Evening class, 17:30-18:30 Travel to campus, 12:00-13:00 Lunch and transition, 08:00-12:00 Part-time work; Thu 2026-11-05: 18:30-21:30 Evening class, 17:30-18:30 Travel to campus, 16:30-17:30 Physical activity, 12:00-13:00 Lunch and transition; Fri 2026-11-06: 12:00-13:00 Lunch and transition, 08:00-12:00 Part-time work), which weekdays, time windows, and end date work for your study sessions?",
      "choices": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "question",
      "id": "workload",
      "groupId": "intake",
      "text": "What weekly study hours target, maximum 1-hour sessions per day, and break duration (minutes) between same-day blocks work best?",
      "choices": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "answer",
      "questionId": "availability",
      "text": "For these two weeks, Wednesday, Thursday and Friday from 14:00 to 16:15 can work when the calendar is clear. I prefer to keep the weekend open."
    },
    {
      "kind": "answer",
      "questionId": "workload",
      "text": "Four study hours a week feels workable, with no more than two sessions a day and a 15-minute break between them."
    },
